eoretical and computational results, we demonstrate that $\\texttt{$\\ell_2$-norm-diag}$ recovers nodes with sufficiently strong cluster membership in graph instances generated by the NFM, thereby making progress towards establishing the provable robustness of our proposed algorithm.\n\nFull-text Links:View paper on--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInformationen über die Geschwindigkeitskontrolle in Verl-Kaunitz - FragDenStaat (https://fragdenstaat.de/anfrage/informationen-ueber-die-geschwindigkeitskontrolle-in-verl-kaunitz/)\nciteturn1search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: 3 weeks ago;     Informationen über die Geschwindigkeitskontrolle in Verl-Kaunitz [#352259]\n\n# Informationen über die Geschwindigkeitskontrolle in Verl-Kaunitz\n\nAnfrage an: Kreisverwaltung Gütersloh\n\nalle Informationen zur Geschwindigkeitskontrolle am Ortsausgang von Verl-Kaunitz am 24. September 2025 insbesondere Eich- und Messprotokolle.\n\n### Anfrage eingeschlafen\n\nWarte auf Antwort\n\n  * Datum\n\n27. Oktober 2025\n\n  * Frist\n\n29. November 2025\n\n  * Anfrage folgen? Anfrage folgen? 0 Follower\n\n  * Korrespondenz 1\n\n  * ### Franz Purucker\n\nam 27.10.2025\n\nAntrag nach dem Informationsfreiheitsgesetz NRW, UIG NRW, VIG Guten Tag, bitte senden Sie mir Folgendes zu: al…\n\nAn Kreisverwaltung Gütersloh Details\n\nVon\n    Franz Purucker\nBetreff\n    Informationen über die Geschwindigkeitskontrolle in Verl-Kaunitz [#352259]\nDatum\n    27. Oktober 2025 14:57\nAn\n    Kreisverwaltung Gütersloh\nStatus\n    Warte auf Antwort — E-Mail wurde erfolgreich versendet.\n\nAntrag nach dem Informationsfreiheitsgesetz NRW, UIG NRW, VIG Guten Tag, bitte senden Sie mir Folgendes zu:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe NFM positive-semidefinite subgraph conjecture under Dirichlet noise | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/352259/the-nfm-positive-semidefinite-subgraph-conjecture-under-diri)\nciteturn1search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; The NFM positive-semidefinite subgraph conjecture under Dirichlet noise ... There exists a scalar $t(k,\\bm{\\alpha})\\in(0.5,1/\\sqrt{2})$t(k,α)∈(0.5,1/2​) such that, for every $j\\in[k]$j∈[k], $G[V_j']$G[V j′​] satisfies the hypothesis of Theorem 2 with probability not converging to $0$0 as $n\\to\\infty$n→∞. ... Jimit Majmudar and Stephen Vavasis, “Robust Correlation Clustering with Asymmetric Noise”, arXiv:2110.08385 (2021).\n\nThe NFM positive-semidefinite subgraph conjecture under Dirichlet noise\n\nLet $G=(V,W)$G=(V,W) be generated using the node-feature model (NFM), with simplex distribution given by a Dirichlet distribution with constant parameter $\\bm{\\alpha}$α. For $j\\in[k]$j∈[k], define\n\n$$V_j':= \\{i\\in[n]:\\theta^i_j\\geq t(k,\\bm{\\alpha})\\}.$$V j′​:={i∈[n]:θ j i​≥t(k,α)}.\n\nNFM positive-semidefinite subgraph conjecture. There exists a scalar $t(k,\\bm{\\alpha})\\in(0.5,1/\\sqrt{2})$t(k,α)∈(0.5,1/2​) such that, for every $j\\in[k]$j∈[k], $G[V_j']$G[V j′​] satisfies the hypothesis of Theorem 2 with probability not converging to $0$0 as $n\\to\\infty$n→∞.\n\nHere $G[V_j']$G[V j′​] is the subgraph induced by the nodes whose $j$j th feature is at least the threshold. The conjecture is motivated by experiments suggesting that the relevant Laplacians remain positive semidefinite with nonvanishing probability, potentially enabling recovery on suitably selected strong-node subgraphs.\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\nSources & references View supporting material\n\n## Primary source\n\nJimit Majmudar and Stephen Vavasis, “Robust Correlation Clustering with Asymmetric Noise”, arXiv:2110.08385 (2021).\n\ncorrelation-clusteringspectral-graph-theorystochastic-models\n\n0\n\n1 week ago\n\n## Solutions 0\n\nSign in to post a solution.\n\n[Button: Solve w